<title>FRANCE: Bull share sale at 34-39 Ffr/shr - papers.</title>
<headline>Bull share sale at 34-39 Ffr/shr - papers.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The third stage of the privatisation of Cie des Machines Bull, through the sale by the state of 19 million shares, will take place at a price of between 34 and 39 francs per share, French newspapers said.</p>
<p>The price will be announced on Tuesday evening.</p>
<p>The papers quoted Bull chairman Jean-marie Descarpentries as saying &quot;the price should be between 34 and 39 francs and the sale will yield the state half a billion of francs.&quot;</p>
<p>Bull shares are suspened pending the operation.</p>
<p>Descarpentries was quoted as saying Bull could sell its 19.2 percent stake in Packard-Bell NEC.</p>
<p>A 4.9 percent stake in Wang could also be sold.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
